## Validation gates

This document defines validation scope and cadence for compiler and documentation
work. Choose checks by branch, checkpoint and changed behaviour. Feature-branch
iteration uses targeted checks, important boundaries use routine validation and
merge readiness uses the full gate.

### Task-reading guide for validation

Start every completion decision with `Choose the final gate by scope`. Heading
paths use `>` to name nested sections. Read the selected heading through the
next heading of the same or higher level, including nested subsections unless
the route narrows further. Read this document in full when changing validation
infrastructure or auditing the complete gate policy.

[table:
    [th:
        [: **Task**]
        [: **Read**]
    ]

    [td:
        [: Select checks for a branch commit or merge checkpoint]
        [: `Choose the final gate by scope`]
    ]

    [td:
        [: Choose direct compiler or Cargo invocation]
        [: `Compiler invocation` and `Shared Cargo defaults`]
    ]

    [td:
        [: Complete or review code-bearing work]
        [:
            - `Code-bearing final gate`
            - `Formatting`
            - `Manual architecture audits` when its trigger applies
            - `Progress-matrix review`
            - `Benchmark safety`
            - `Failure handling`
            - `Code-bearing completion checklist`
        ]
    ]

    [td:
        [: Complete or review documentation-only work]
        [:
            - `Documentation-only release-build gate`
            - `Generated documentation`
            - `Failure handling`
            - `Documentation-only completion checklist`
        ]
    ]

    [td:
        [: Add or change a Cargo feature, or a feature-gated test]
        [: `Feature lanes`]
    ]

    [td:
        [: Add or change a broad-source architecture ban]
        [: `Source audit`]
    ]

    [td:
